RICCI FLOW 
→ 516.37 → Differential Geometry

CONTEXT
  fundamental geometry; Ricci flow is a prime example.

CORE EQUATION
  ∂g / ∂t  =  -2 Ric(g)

  g     Riemannian metric tensor on manifold M
  Ric   Ricci curvature tensor of g
  t     flow parameter (time)
  M     smooth n-manifold

FUNDAMENTALS
  Type          Riemannian metric flow (nonlinear parabolic PDE)
  Analogy       heat equation on the metric
  Short-time    existence + uniqueness (Hamilton 1982)
  Behavior      smooths irregular curvature toward
                constant-curvature or model geometries
  Singularities finite-time pinch-offs; blow-ups are
                Ricci solitons or shrinking spheres / cigars
  Normalization volume-preserving variant adds scalar
                curvature term so average volume stays 1

HISTORICAL ROLE
  Hamilton      introduced the flow to attack curvature
  Perelman      2002–03 entropy + reduced-length tools
                proved Poincaré conjecture and
                Thurston geometrization conjecture
  8 geometries  S³, E³, H³, S²×R, H²×R, SL̃(2,R), Nil, Sol
